=== PR l.411
- **(b) THE LOOK.** ONE patrol leaves its round for ONE week (`looking`; the round's lowest-priority stretch loses its rider — the cost) and goes to the place (the light-unit physics; a look farther than one hop is a converging week first). It reads what is there BY THE WORLD'S OWN BELIEF RULES: a site's holder (ST; a site under the court veil — `keptSecret`, ST §2.4 — is found only with a keyed draw, `LOOK_FIND_SECRET` 0.3), a menace's tracks (MN), a body (THE BODIES), the party's traces (PT's deed at the place in the last season, if its `proof` is `shown` or `spoken` — PT §11's visibility), or NOTHING. Seeded (stream `patrol:look:<settlementId>:<placeKey>:<tick>`). A FINDING IS A SIGHTING, written ONCE at the tick of seeing into the ONE belief of that holder's might — through ST's one writer as the site's `seenBy` entry with the might BAND seen then, for a MENACE holder into MN's belief, for a BODY into BD's (RULINGS-ROUND4 A.17: "a patrol's look" refreshes it; "never a live truth read, never a second belief") — and a kept-secret den found by a look is the at-hand court's WITNESS (A.16); the veil itself is lifted only by ST's `made_known`, never by the riders; PR keeps no belief of its own [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — A.16 · A.17 (the PR half: the look as a sighting producer) · BD's route (6): the r3 `hidden` was ST's withdrawn word (ST §2.4: "the compile's `hidden`/`revealed` WITHDRAWN (the map's PARTY secrecy states)") and is now also THE BODIES' `hiddenWays` homonym, so the constant is renamed `LOOK_FIND_SECRET` (FREE, `tokens-r4.out`)].
